        "image": "shopify://shop_images/portrait-artist.jpg",
        "heading": "My story",
        "lead": "<p>I'm Andrea Bowman, an artist working in Cape Town. I trained at the Metafora Art School in Barcelona, and my work has appeared in five magazines, in homes where top designers have used my art.</p>",
        "text": "<p>I am a typical artist: untidy, full of product and unable to stop. I love what I make, then I can't live with it, and after a month I love it all over again.</p>"
      }
    },
    "how_i_work": {
      "type": "narrow-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Making is a psychological process. It passes through pathways that take you out of your norm and into the moment. Only the moment counts until you finally stop, and it goes on for days.</p><p>Then my brain swaps from the creative space to the admin space, and it is all organisation and finishing touches for the framers and the other people who support me. Whatever I am involved in, I cannot stop until I have got where I need to be with the piece or the creation at hand.</p>"
          }
        },
        "quote_1": {
          "type": "quote",
          "settings": {
            "quote": "I have a determined ambition in art, yet I know I need to constantly grow and improve."
          }
        },
        "text_2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>It is that dedication that keeps me going, otherwise it plays with your mind. Either you feel you are posturing and it is not worthy, or you suddenly feel high and know it is flowing.</p><p>After returning from Oman, besides the amazing photography, I had to create the huge Omani pots I wanted. Each pot took five men to move into place and will outlive me. They are nearly as large as I am.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
